1
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:12,100
Back up, restore, archive — Settings ▸ System — Backup is for disaster. Archive is for age. They are not the same job.

2
00:00:17,388 --> 00:00:23,446
Settings ▸ Backup & Restore takes a full copy of the clinic’s data — three places to put it.

3
00:00:23,446 --> 00:00:30,395
Local downloads a file to this machine. Google Drive and OneDrive push it to the cloud account you connected.

4
00:00:30,395 --> 00:00:40,932
A cloud destination that has not been connected cannot be used — the button says so rather than failing later.

5
00:00:40,932 --> 00:00:52,035
The backup is every table: patients, appointments, clinical records, claims, settings.

6
00:00:52,035 --> 00:00:58,745
Accounting and Inventory also take their own module backups — useful before a big change to just one of them.

7
00:00:58,745 --> 00:01:06,587
Restore reads a backup file back in. Read the warning: this replaces current data, and it cannot be undone.

8
00:01:06,587 --> 00:01:17,866
Which is why a restore is a decision made deliberately, on a quiet system, not a thing tried during clinic.

9
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:27,061
Archive solves the opposite problem. Backup is for losing data; archive is for data you must keep but no longer work with.

10
00:01:27,061 --> 00:01:34,357
Old appointments, closed claims, audit history — out of the working tables, still fully retrievable.

11
00:01:34,357 --> 00:01:42,599
And read the note: restoring an archive merges. Duplicates are detected and skipped, so nothing is lost.

12
00:01:42,599 --> 00:01:50,781
Automatic archive rules run on a schedule — closed claims after twenty-four months, audit logs after twenty-four.

13
00:01:50,781 --> 00:02:02,609
Set the retention your regulator asks for once, and nobody has to remember it again.

14
00:02:02,609 --> 00:02:13,833
You can browse an archive without restoring it — table by table, row by row.

15
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:23,347
So: back up for disaster, archive for age. Two problems, two tools — and both of them scheduled, not remembered.

16
00:02:24,829 --> 00:02:41,169
